  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the main uncertainty is whether RNA alone provides a useful predictive baseline and how strong a simple reference configuration is. config_001 tests an RNA-only, single-profile PCA baseline, isolating the RNA representation without confounding effects from profile aggregation, image encoding, or fusion. It is the best first experiment because it is simple, likely low-cost, establishes a lower-bound reference for later RNA encoder and profile comparisons, and avoids prematurely assuming that multimodal or multiprofile models will be better."
